# 5 — Pagefile (virtual memory) — set to 2–4 GB (safe)

**Manual GUI (safe, recommended):**

* Win key → type **Performance** → “Adjust the appearance and performance of Windows” → Advanced → Virtual memory → Change.
* Uncheck “Automatically manage pagefile size for all drives”. Select your C: drive → Custom size. Set **Initial size = 2048 MB**, **Maximum size = 4096 MB** (2–4 GB), then Set → OK → reboot.

This is reversible and safe. It gives Windows more virtual room without hardware changes.

